---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy: ForeverQR makes zero requests"
  description="What runs where: everything runs in your browser. No analytics, no fonts or scripts from other sites, the camera stays local, only localStorage is used."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold sm:text-4xl">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-lg">ForeverQR has no back end. Nothing you type, upload or scan is sent anywhere.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">What runs where</h2>
    <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 leading-7">
      <li>QR codes are drawn in your browser, by JavaScript that ships with this site. Your text, Wi-Fi password or contact details never leave the page.</li>
      <li>PNG, SVG and PDF files are built in your browser and handed to you as a download.</li>
      <li>Reading a QR code (the checker) uses a decoder compiled to WebAssembly that also ships with this site. Uploaded images stay in memory.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">Zero outside requests</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-7">
      Fonts, scripts, styles and images all come from this site. There are no analytics, no ads, no tag managers and no
      content networks. A Content Security Policy tells your browser to refuse anything else, and the meter in the footer
      counts the requests this page made so you can see for yourself. To check by hand, open your browser's DevTools, switch to the Network tab and reload: every row is from this site.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">The camera</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-7">
      The checker can use your camera to read a code. Video frames are decoded on your device and are never recorded or
      uploaded. The camera starts only when you press the Camera button and stops when you press Stop or leave the page.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">What is stored</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-7">
      Your studio settings (and your logo, if it is small) are saved in your browser's localStorage so they are there next
      time. The theme choice is saved the same way. There are no cookies. The Reset button clears the saved settings.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-bold">The one optional outbound step</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 leading-7">
      When the checker finds a link that goes through a redirect service, it can offer to open that link so you can see
      where it ends up. That happens only after you confirm in a dialog, in a new tab, and it is a normal visit to that
      site, which may count the scan. Cancel and nothing is requested.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
